    <item>
      <title>Boris, the friendly Bokoblin</title>
      <author>Deano309</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/723383</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/723383#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">9281c19c16275a778c6dadde202d60a13f69ea98</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:21:13 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac0780ee457a.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac337bf27ca3.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac0780e9f794.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; Update&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Bugfix&lt;/em&gt;: Fixed Boris' attacks not registering if loading game with Champion's Leathers already equipped.&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Improvement&lt;/em&gt;: Increased stats and enemy detection for armored version.&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boris, the friendly Bokoblin.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Boris is a young Bokoblin who has dreams of becoming more than his brethren.&lt;br&gt;As he was growing up, he heard stories of a Legendary Hylian warrior, who was the sworn enemy of his people.&lt;br&gt;But, despite all others of his kind fearing or hating this warrior, Boris was filled with awe.&lt;br&gt;He thought of the warrior as a hero, so left his people in search of becoming the Warrior's student.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You will find him waiting around outside Lookout Landing, hoping to be recruited.&lt;br&gt;Once recruited, he can be summoned to your side by &lt;b&gt;whistling&lt;/b&gt; (And dismissed using button combo "&lt;b&gt;ZL+A&lt;/b&gt;").&lt;br&gt;When you require assistance, he will provide what help he can...&lt;br&gt;Although small, his bravery cannot be faulted as he will charge into battle without any consideration as to what he is facing.&lt;br&gt;As a young student, he lacks discipline and focus (Sometimes he is busy daydreaming until an enemy wanders directly in front of him, and he also often runs off to chase wildlife!).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;HOWEVER&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;, if you are wearing the Champion's Leathers, he becomes an inspired and focused ally.&lt;br&gt;With increased health, strength, enemy detection, armor plating and improved sword &amp; shield, he &lt;i&gt;can&lt;/i&gt; make a real difference in battle.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;He won't follow your path when you leave, instead he will remain watchful in the area you last summoned him.&lt;br&gt;He has a lot to learn and, maybe one day, if he is lucky enough, he can fulfil his dream of becoming as strong as a &lt;i&gt;real&lt;/i&gt; Sage!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Notes:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;This modifies the Player.brain.root and is not compatible with any other mod that also edits this.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Boris is not permitted to follow you whilst you're inside Shrines.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;TKMM required for installing and only tested on TotK v1.2.1&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/boris_the_friendly_bokoblin_102b.zip" type="application/zip"/>
      <category>NPC</category>
      <category>Models</category>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>BotW Abilities</title>
      <author>HanSoloBlaster</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/726588</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/726588#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">70956d83d277f0b9a3509447fae5c6ede7fe7016</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:30:38 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6acb8ef6c86e8.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6acb8ef791a94.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ace9c11c06ef.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ace9c2d77ea1.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6acb8ef60bdae.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6acb8ef7d4e83.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6acb8ef791359.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6acb8ef732d57.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;BotW Abilities&lt;/h1&gt;Adds Stasis, Cryonis and Remote Bombs from BotW to TotK. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Note that these are merely shoddy approximations of the original abilities. They &lt;b&gt;don't&lt;/b&gt; have the exact appearance and behavior of the originals. Also please respect that this is essentially an &lt;b&gt;alpha version&lt;/b&gt; of the mod. There will be bugs and the user experience isn't currently great. I intend to fix these things. &lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Recent changes:&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;b&gt;v0.1.4&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Higher fidelity remote bombs thanks to an anonymous contributor. &lt;br&gt;- Reduce memory usage on Switch from ~8 MiB to ~3 MiB by using RomFS glow on bombs and stasis (again, from a contributor who wishes to remain anonymous).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;v0.1.3&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Updated mod to &lt;b&gt;add a second page to the ability wheel&lt;/b&gt; to access Cryonis and Stasis. &lt;b&gt;Access it by holding L1, then tapping R1&lt;/b&gt;. The old method of activation no longer works. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;v0.1.2&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Update mod to &lt;b&gt;support Ryujinx/Ryubing and Switch hardware&lt;/b&gt;. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3&gt;v0.1.1&lt;/h3&gt;- Change subsdk slot from 5 to 7 to avoid overlap with my Zonai Hookshot mod. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;How to use&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stasis&lt;/b&gt;: hold L1, then tap R1 and select cryonis from the second ability page to enter preview mode. Press A over an object to freeze it for ten seconds (enemies for five). Afterward, subsequent hits to objects will build momentum as it works in BotW. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Remote Bomb&lt;/b&gt;: The sphere and cube bomb now show at the front of your materials quick view and materials in the main menu. Hold, throw or fuse them to arrows. Tap L to detonate. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cryonis&lt;/b&gt;: hold L1, then tap R1 and select cryonis from the second ability page to activate preview mode. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Abilities act like native TotK abilities - the most recent ability is accessed with a tap of "L".&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Requires Tears of the Kingdom 1.2.1.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Emulator&lt;/b&gt;: extract the archive and copy its `BotW Abilities` folder into the game's mod folder, then enable it in the add-on list. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Switch&lt;/b&gt;: copy the 0100F2C0115B6000 folder into atmosphere/contents/.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Known Issues&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stasis:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Objects sometimes continue to rotate or fall under stasis&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Target/selection often requires you to be very close.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Selection often doesn't appear even when close, or flickers in and out.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Stasis' "arrow" showing magnitude and direction of momentum is fairly inaccurate to the BotW version. It mostly updates in a straight line based on Link's forward position and doesn't update based on angle of weapon attack like in BotW&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Stasis doesn't work on many enemies and some passive "enemies" including constructs and the blue bunny. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Stasis will appear to work on an enemey in selection, but in practice they don't actually freeze. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Development&lt;/h2&gt;Developed and tested on the Citron emulator, Ryubing and Switch hardware. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;All (freely MIT licensed) source code and a more detailed README.md can be found &lt;a href="https://github.com/afiaka87/totk-mods/tree/main/botw-abilities" target="_blank"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;AI Disclaimer&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This project was developed with heavy help from AI Claude Opus 5.5 and Sol 6.1. For an overview of how I develop ExeFS mods using AI please see this post &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/posts/13964739"&gt;https://gamebanana.com/posts/13964739&lt;/a&gt;.</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/botw-abilities-v010-emulator-subsdk5.zip" type="application/zip"/>
